> f(x: u8) = x/(x-1)
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires x - 1 != 0  (in x/(x - 1))
  defined at 255 of 256 points
  defined for: 0, 2..255
  undefined e.g. at x=1
  C undefined behaviour at 1 points, e.g. x=1
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range f
range of f -> u8:
  0..2   (3 distinct values)
  values: 0..2
  fits in u2
  undefined at 1 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> wrap f
wrap analysis of f:
  x - 1   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=0
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=128
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 256 points of the domain
> equiv f f
f and f are equal on the domain of f (exhaustive)
